mperature, and charging losses matter.","57":", I'd choose the Anker C","56":"home emergency backup","50":"9 hours","54":"What I'd buy","48":"14 hours","51":"400W","47":"200W","52":"7 hours","55":"For ","49":"320W"}},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/fallbackMarkdown","o":"replace","v":"# Best 2,000Wh solar generator kits with panels (2026)\n\nFor a solar generator kit around **2,000Wh (2kWh)**, I'd prioritize battery longevity, inverter output, solar charging speed, warranty, and the total price including panels.\n\nOne important distinction: **2,000Wh is battery capacity**, while **2,000W is power output**\\. For a useful home backup or camping kit, I'd look for approximately 2,000Wh of capacity, at least 2,000W of AC output, and 200\u2013400W or more of solar panels.\n\n## My top 5 kits from current search results\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn585948product0\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n(Best overall value)\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn585948product0\",\"Anker SOLIX C2000X Gen 2 (2,048Wh) Solar Generator w/ 200W B\u2026\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$1,199.99\n\n2,048Wh \u00b7 2,400W AC \u00b7 200W solar panel\n\nExcellent balance of power, efficiency, and portability. The panel is modest, but the kit is competitively priced.\n\nSeller: Lowe's\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn585948product27\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n(Best lower-cost option)\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn585948product27\",\"EcoFlow Delta 3 Max 2400/3400W 2kWh Portable Power Station w\u2026\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$1,099.00\n\n2,048Wh \u00b7 2,400W AC \u00b7 160W panel\n\nStrong value for emergency backup. You'll likely want additional panels for regular solar charging.\n\nSeller: The Home Depot\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn585948product5\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn585948product5\",\"Jackery Solar Generator 2000 v2 + 400W solar\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$1,399.00\n\n2,042Wh \u00b7 2,200W AC \u00b7 2 \u00d7 200W panels\n\nMy preferred configuration for camping and off-grid use when you need a more practical solar array.\n\nSeller: Eco Solar Kits\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn585948product4\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn585948product4\",\"EcoFlow DELTA 2 Max + 320W solar\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$1,499.00\n\n2,048Wh \u00b7 2,400W AC \u00b7 2 \u00d7 160W panels\n\nA versatile choice with expandable battery capacity and up to 1,000W solar input.\n\nSeller: The Home Depot\n\n---\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"entity_refs\":[\"turn585948product1\"],\"aspect_ratio\":\"1:1\",\"layout\":\"carousel\",\"num_per_query\":1}\ue201\n\n**\ue200entity\ue202[\"turn585948product1\",\"Anker SOLIX C2000 Gen 2 + 400W solar\"]\ue201**\n\n## \\$1,999.99\n\n2,048Wh \u00b7 2,400W AC \u00b7 400W solar panel\n\nBest considered if you specifically want the Anker ecosystem and a manufacturer-direct bundle.\n\nSeller: Ankersolix US\n\nPrices are observed listings from the November 13, 2026 search, in USD. Promotions, shipping, and inventory can change.\n\n## Solar charging comparison\n\nApproximate time to recharge a 2kWh battery from empty, assuming good sunlight and 75% effective panel output\\:\n\n| Included solar | Estimated peak-sun hours |\n|--------|--------|\n| 160W | 17 hours |\n| 200W | 14 hours |\n| 320W | 9 hours |\n| 400W | 7 hours |\n\nThese are cumulative peak-sun hours, not elapsed daylight hours. Weather, shading, temperature, and charging losses matter.\n\n## What I'd buy\n\nFor **home emergency backup**, I'd choose the Anker C"}],"c":11}       

